From 5a77e5a0a80286ce41b066d41bce3025735b9c84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:54:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace made-up stat counters with Process Nodes +
 Application Fields

The "V-Chip at a glance" counters (75+ engineers, 400+ years combined
experience, 200+ project releases) were flagged as concerning since
those figures were estimates, not real numbers. Replaces them with
two factual-shaped capability lists instead: supported process nodes
(2nm through 24nm, as badges) and application fields served
(Automotive, Communication, Industrial, Consumer Electronics,
Computer & Storage, IoT & Wearables, Medical, each with an icon),
adapted from the reference layout and notes provided.

Renamed the icon list's class from .application-list to .field-list
after finding it collided with an existing, differently-styled
.application-list component used elsewhere on the site (the
applications-panel on service pages) -- would have silently inherited
that component's bordered-pill styling otherwise.

Also removed the now-orphaned stat-counter CSS and its count-up
IntersectionObserver logic in site.js, since nothing references
data-count-to anymore.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
